  "conclusions": [
    "Anonymous births remove the severe counted name inheritance observed with only six initial masks in the two later exposed panels; this is a meaningful causal control, not a held-out result.",
    "The full criterion still fails: final coverage1077/1799=.5986659 is below.60. Pooled coverage does not replace the perpanel criterion.",
    "The optimistic eight-seed initialization has substantially higher middle/final coverage; automatic discovery does not yet reproduce its performance.",
    "First errors471 and1230 have essentially the same geometry and accepted name in allthree arms, so they are not newly caused by birth insertion.",
    "At996 the three arms produce broadly similar large geometry but only births crosses the fixed.7qualitygate (p10.7148 versus.5139six/.6548eight). Its strict error cannot be excused from the visual diagnostic.",
    "The three selected examples show localization/extent ambiguity and no established initial seed contamination or biological swap. They do not establish that all23unmatched names are semantically correct.",
    "These unknown calves were already visible at startup. Keep the separate physical-entrant failure/control, deletion/reentry limitations and all previous failed results."
  ]
